---
source: crates/aidp-cli/tests/cli_surface.rs
expression: normalized
---
Cost measurement: per-run breakdown, JSONL ledger, counterfactual and anomaly detection. Never changes a `model:` or makes a routing decision

Usage: <BIN> cost [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  show            Cost of one run by stage and model plus the total, always paired with its provenance (`jsonl` | `budget` | `unavailable`), never a silent 0
  ledger          Append one numeric JSONL line per sub-agent to the durable routing ledger (default `<vault>/Knowledge/<repo>/_routing/decisions.jsonl`); write failures are swallowed
  counterfactual  Replay this run's observed token volumes at an alternate tier's prices. Cost only: says nothing about the alternate model's quality
  ticket          Token cost of one ticket from the daemon (flows, steps, stages, models, window share); `--format footer` prints the one-line report footer instead
  anomaly         Flag cost outliers via the Iglewicz-Hoaglin modified z-score (median + MAD). Exits 6 (negative verdict) if an outlier is found
  help            Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --workspace-root <PATH>
          Workspace to act on instead of the current directory

      --vault <PATH>
          Obsidian vault to use instead of `AIDP_VAULT`, `~/.aidp/config.json` or auto-detection

      --no-vault
          Ignore any vault and keep artefacts in the repo (`.aidp/pipelines/`)

      --no-knowledge
          Leave the compile-time `## Knowledge` block out of the stage prompts

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format. Each command keeps its own default when omitted

          Possible values:
          - json-compact: One compact JSON document on a single line
          - json-pretty:  One indented JSON document
          - ndjson:       One compact JSON value per line
          - text:         Human-readable text
          - footer:       The one-line cost footer of a report, for `<BIN> cost ticket`; text elsewhere

  -v, --verbose...
          More diagnostics on stderr; repeat for more (`-vv`)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
